# SPA history-API fallback.
#
# The app uses BrowserRouter, so /logbook, /calls, /hospital?tab=schedules and
# every other route exists only in the client bundle. Netlify serves the publish
# directory as static files, so a hard load or a refresh on any of those paths
# looks for a file that was never built and answers 404. The notification
# routing depends on exactly these deep links working from a cold load.
#
# The two vercel.json files in this repo declared this same rewrite, and Netlify
# does not read them.
#
# This file is not build configuration: Vite copies public/ verbatim into the
# publish directory, and the rule below only describes routing. It sets no build
# command, publish directory or plugin, so it cannot conflict with whatever is
# configured in the Netlify dashboard. It is also inert on any other host.
#
# 200 (rewrite), not 301/302: the browser must keep the requested URL so the
# router can read the path and the query string.
/*    /index.html   200
